From: NEURAX-FX <234716687+NEURAX-FX@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] panvk/wsi: present Wayland through linux-dmabuf on kbase

kbase devices are WSI "sw" devices: every present reads the image back on
the CPU and copies it into a wl_shm buffer, which the compositor uploads
again. kbase dma-heap BOs can be exported, so keep the CPU readback for X11
(MIT-SHM; Xvfb/Termux:X11 cannot import them) and present Wayland through
zwp_linux_dmabuf_v1 with the existing dma-buf implicit-sync bridge.

- wsi_device_options::wayland_dmabuf / wsi_device::wayland.dmabuf: Wayland
  ignores wsi->sw (MESA_VK_WSI_DEBUG=sw still forces wl_shm).
- GetMemoryFdKHR is resolved for such devices; the sw present-time fence
  wait and the implicit-sync semaphore only apply to the matching image
  type, so X11 CPU swapchains keep their old behaviour.
- PanVK enables it for kbase unless PANVK_KBASE_DRI3 already selects the
  full dma-buf path; PANVK_WSI_WAYLAND_DMABUF=0 restores wl_shm.

MT6989 (G720, niri-anland -> Anland, 2392x1080 Zink glmark2-es2-wayland):
wl_shm 103-134 -> linux-dmabuf 282-420 fps; 0 torn/mixed frames over 1781
consumer-checked frames.

Generated-by: LLM
---
diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_wsi.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_wsi.c
index f7ff544..3f89e8f 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_wsi.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_wsi.c
@@ -724,6 +724,21 @@ panvk_wsi_init(struct panvk_physical_device *physical_device)
       kbase_kmod_supports_dmabuf(physical_device->kmod.dev);
 #else
       false;
+#endif
+   /* The CPU readback (sw) path copies every frame twice on Wayland: GPU
+    * image -> readback buffer -> wl_shm, then the compositor uploads the SHM
+    * buffer again.  kbase dma-heap BOs can be shared with the compositor
+    * instead (MT6989 niri/Anland, 2392x1080 glmark2: ~100-135 -> 280-420), so
+    * Wayland uses linux-dmabuf while X11 keeps MIT-SHM, whose servers
+    * (Xvfb, Termux:X11) cannot import these buffers.
+    * PANVK_WSI_WAYLAND_DMABUF=0 restores wl_shm. */
+   const bool wayland_dmabuf =
+#if defined(HAVE_PAN_KMOD_KBASE)
+      uses_kbase && !kbase_dmabuf &&
+      debug_get_bool_option("PANVK_WSI_WAYLAND_DMABUF", true) &&
+      kbase_kmod_supports_dmabuf(physical_device->kmod.dev);
+#else
+      false;
 #endif
    VkResult result;
 
@@ -737,6 +752,7 @@ panvk_wsi_init(struct panvk_physical_device *physical_device)
                                 * fourth image when the server is Xwayland. */
                                .extra_xwayland_image =
                                   kbase_dmabuf && kbase_raw_dri3,
+                               .wayland_dmabuf = wayland_dmabuf,
                             });
    if (result != VK_SUCCESS)
       return result;
@@ -754,7 +770,7 @@ panvk_wsi_init(struct panvk_physical_device *physical_device)
     * Termux:X11/Winlator private raw-FD modifier instead of DRM modifiers.
     */
    physical_device->wsi_device.supports_modifiers =
-      !uses_kbase || (kbase_dmabuf && !kbase_raw_dri3);
+      !uses_kbase || (kbase_dmabuf && !kbase_raw_dri3) || wayland_dmabuf;
    physical_device->wsi_device.can_present_on_device =
       panvk_can_present_on_device;
 
